---
description: Production readiness standards for ChefPro
alwaysApply: true
---

# Production Readiness

- Never use filesystem for persistent storage; use Supabase Storage via `src/lib/supabase.ts`.
- Compliance-critical mutations must write audit events in the same Prisma transaction.
- Permission checks on the server must use freshly-fetched user context, never JWT cache.
- All user-facing errors must be caught and shown via toast, never silent 500s.

# Infrastructure

- Database: PostgreSQL via Supabase (configured through `DATABASE_URL`).
- File uploads: Supabase Storage bucket `tasting-photos`.
- Schema changes: Always use `prisma migrate dev`, never `db push` in production.
- Use native PostgreSQL types (Int[], String[], Json) instead of CSV string workarounds.

# Data Fetching

- Use SWR hooks (`src/lib/hooks/use-fetch.ts`) for client-side data, not raw useEffect+fetch.
- Use `mutate()` from SWR after mutations for instant UI refresh.
